node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mH0xu","user":{"login":"theXYZT","id":172810,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3MjgxMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/172810?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT","html_url":"https://github.com/theXYZT","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/theXYZT/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-08T16:44:12Z","updated_at":"2025-04-08T16:44:12Z","body":"> Side note, iteration on `get_key_at_index` is actually $O(n \\log{n})$, not $O(N^2)$, i think. This is because it starts fast and gets slower at the edges :)\r\n\r\nIt should still be $O(N^2)$, just twice as fast. If you think about how many elements we traverse during the loop (1, 2, 3, 4 ...), the sum scales as the square.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2787069038/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2787220452","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104082#issuecomment-2787220452","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104082","id":2787220452,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6mIZvk","user":{"login":"kleonc","id":9283098,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkyODMwOTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9283098?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc","html_url":"https://github.com/kleonc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-08T17:47:03Z","updated_at":"2025-04-08T17:47:03Z","body":"> > Side note, iteration on `get_key_at_index` is actually $O(n \\log{n})$, not $O(N^2)$, i think. This is because it starts fast and gets slower at the edges :)\r\n>\r\n> It should still be $O(N^2)$, just twice as fast. If you think about how many elements we traverse during the loop (1, 2, 3, 4 ...), the sum scales as the square.\r\n\r\nFor formality:\r\n$f(n) = 1 + 2 + ... + n = \\sum_{k=1}^n k = \\frac{1}{2}n(n+1)$\r\n\r\n$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\frac{f(n)}{n \\log{n}} = \\infty$, so $f(n)$ is not $O(n \\log{n})$.\r\n\r\n$\\lim_{n\\to\\infty} \\frac{f(n)}{n^2} = \\frac{1}{2} < \\infty$, so $f(n)$ is $O(n^2)$.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2787220452/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2787223057","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104082#issuecomment-278